  "name": "PersonaCUABench: Benchmarking Computer-Use Agents Serving Diverse Personas",
  "notes": "Reviewed the complete retained abstract and selected exact-v1 construction, evaluation and limitations sections. Main interactions and satisfaction ratings use LLM-simulated personas; human annotators validate selected outputs. The harness observes page text, with screenshots only for auditing. Results are not evidence about real demographic populations or desktop agents. No independent reproduction.",
  "published_at": "2026-10-16",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "PersonaCUABench varies simulated user requests and clarification dialogue over fixed web tasks, comparing task completion with requirement handling and persona-agent satisfaction ratings.",
